Social Hub - Oman — Website Requirements Specification (WRS)
Project Overview & Ownership
Platform Name: Social Hub - Oman
Business Owners: M Zuhaib Tariq, M Fareed Tariq
Core Functionality: A high-end digital subscription marketplace. Upon opening the website, users land directly on the Subscription Services catalog with default Oman (OMR) pricing. Features full bilingual support (English & Arabic with LTR/RTL switching), direct WhatsApp order dispatch across two dedicated support lines, and a complaint submission module delivering directly to global2stor2@gmail.com.
Key Functional & Interface Requirements
1. Direct Entry, Fixed Localization & Language Toggle
Direct Access Landing: Opening the URL routes users directly to the Subscription Services catalog without any landing page or pre-entry modals.
Default Target Region:
🇴🇲 Oman (OMR) — All pricing tags display directly in Omani Rial (OMR).
Bilingual Switcher (Top-Right Placement):
Location: Fixed in the top-right corner of the global header navigation bar across all device sizes.
Supported Languages: English (EN) and Arabic (AR / العربية).
Behavior: Dynamic client-side language switching without page reloads, accompanied by full LTR-to-RTL layout transitions when switching to Arabic.
Persistence: Saved in local storage.
2. Homepage & UI/UX Standards
Design Aesthetic: Dark or modern luxury palette, clean bilingual typography (Inter / Tajawal), high-contrast CTA buttons, and smooth micro-interactions.
Core Layout Sections:
Hero Section: High-converting visual showcase highlighting instant digital delivery in Oman.
Brand Introduction: Brief overview establishing marketplace trust under ownership of M Zuhaib Tariq, M Fareed Tariq.
Subscription Catalog Grid: Immediate display of all digital subscription cards with OMR price tags.
Customer Support & WhatsApp Showcase: Highlights direct order routing to dedicated WhatsApp lines.
Global Header & Footer: Persistent layout containers across all pages.
3. Subscription Catalog
The storefront ships with an empty catalog. Names, English/Arabic descriptions, prices, and images are added only through Admin → Add Services after publish. There is no bundled seed list and no backup catalog in source.
Note on Pricing Architecture: Price values stay separate from card body descriptions. Prices render only on the Price Tags / Package Selection Toggles (1 Month vs. 1 Year).
4. Direct WhatsApp Ordering System & Multi-Number Logic
Checkout routes directly to customer support over WhatsApp using two configured support numbers:
Configured Support Numbers:
Line 1: +923254308205
Line 2: +933274596027
Routing Logic: Dynamic distribution (round-robin or sequential fallback) between both numbers.
